WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.520
Congresswoman Debbie McCaskill Powell&nbsp;
represents Florida's twenty sixth district.&nbsp;

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:11.040
She joins me today. Congresswoman, thanks for&nbsp;
being on. I really appreciate your time. Thank you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:19.200
for having me, David. The Florida vote is very,&nbsp;
very interesting. Florida as a state may well&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:26.000
determine who wins the presidential election, Joe&nbsp;
Biden or Donald Trump. And then within Florida,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:32.480
your district may actually signal the way that the&nbsp;
state goes. It's a very interesting district. As&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:38.800
you've mentioned in other conversations, we've&nbsp;
had nearly 70 percent Latino voters. But talk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:44.320
a little bit about the dynamics there in Florida.&nbsp;
What are the most important issues to Floridians?&nbsp;

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:49.600
Well, first, let me say that you're absolutely&nbsp;
correct. I think that the state of Florida&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:53.760
is going to be one of the most&nbsp;
important states in this election.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:59.360
The road to the White House begins in Florida.
And, yes, it starts in Florida's 26 districts.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:04.880
The top issue here has been and continues&nbsp;
to be health care, health care, access.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:11.040
I represent an area where 70 percent of the people&nbsp;
that live in my district are Latinos, Hispanic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:16.560
from the Hispanic community, very diverse&nbsp;
Ecuadorians, Colombians, Argentinians, Mexicans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:22.080
many of them are Cuban-Americans.&nbsp;
And for them, during this pandemic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:27.200
the spin of it has hit us very hard here in&nbsp;
Miami-Dade County. We became the epicenter of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:34.000
of Kofod during the summer. And it's because of&nbsp;
failed leadership locally and at the state level.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:39.200
And many people lost their jobs. They didn't&nbsp;
have access to quality health care. And the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:43.120
stakes of this election have become even&nbsp;
higher now that the Senate is trying to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:48.560
push for that nomination to the Supreme Court. The&nbsp;
Supreme Court, as you know, is going to be hearing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:53.440
the lawsuit to repeal the Affordable&nbsp;
Care Act. And in my district, David,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:57.040
we have the second largest number of people&nbsp;
that get their health care through the ACA.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:02.640
Three hundred thousand individuals in&nbsp;
my district have preexisting conditions.&nbsp;

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:08.880
So if the ACA is repealed, you would see millions&nbsp;
of Americans losing their health coverage and so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:14.640
many here in my district that would lose that. And&nbsp;
I can tell you that the energy in South Florida,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:19.200
it has gone up significantly in the&nbsp;
past few months. People are out there.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:25.040
They're engaged. There are so many grassroots&nbsp;
movements going on in South Florida. They are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:31.040
coming up for me. They're coming out for Biden.&nbsp;
They understand what's at stake at this election.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:35.760
And because of their care, because they know&nbsp;
who's going to protect their care. I think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:42.480
that the energy has really gone way above what&nbsp;
anybody expected within the American electorate.&nbsp;

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:49.760
There are different groups that tend to vote one&nbsp;
way or the other. And as a general rule, three of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:57.520
the most left leaning groups are Jewish Americans,&nbsp;
African-Americans and Latino or Hispanic Americans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:05.280
generally within that last group. Cuban Americans&nbsp;
tend to be the most conservative. And there seems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:09.600
to be this kind of reflexive anti Castro&nbsp;
thing that goes on and that we've seen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:15.360
Can you address a little bit? You know, your&nbsp;
district is the perfect place epicenter to see all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:21.360
of these different groups, as you mentioned, and&nbsp;
their priorities and vote voting interests. Does&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:26.480
this the perspective of the Cuban-American&nbsp;
electorate seem different this time around?&nbsp;

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:33.280
Yeah, and, you know, there is a group of&nbsp;
Cuban-Americans that are very much in favor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:38.720
of Donald Trump. And that's because there has&nbsp;
been a lot of misinformation spread about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:45.600
Democrats there in instigating fear, saying that,&nbsp;
you know, accusing Democrats of being socialist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:50.320
which is completely false. And for Cuban-Americans&nbsp;
and for a lot of people that have fled violent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:55.760
regimes in Latin America. This is scary. And&nbsp;
they've been using that message to divide,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:59.920
to control that vote. But I can tell&nbsp;
you that there is also a significant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:06.080
group of Cuban Americans who are 100 percent&nbsp;
behind Joe Biden. They know that Donald Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:13.040
has been an ally of Vladimir Putin. And let's back&nbsp;
up for a second. Vladimir Putin is propping up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:19.040
the narco regime in Venezuela. The mother regime,&nbsp;
they are propping up Cuba. They are one of their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:25.680
top allies in Cuba. And Trump is standing right&nbsp;
next to them. So Cuban-Americans here in marry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:30.240
many Latin Americans understand that the person&nbsp;
that they need to fear is Donald Trump, because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:36.320
we're seeing so many signs of someone that's&nbsp;
trying to grab onto power, who is doing whatever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:44.240
he can going towards the road of an authoritarian&nbsp;
regime. So Cuban-Americans here are now standing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:49.680
up and saying, no, we do not support Donald&nbsp;
Trump. We are with Biden. There's a group called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:55.040
Gusanos Combined. But there's also Equatoria&nbsp;
notes, nosecone Biden. So how does Joe Biden and.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.040 --> 00:05:02.880
That's been a grass roots movement that has&nbsp;
started really by all the Latin Americans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:06.480
that are living down here that have said&nbsp;
enough, we're not going to follow these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:12.080
guys anymore. So I'm very optimistic and excited&nbsp;
to see what's happening here in South Florida.&nbsp;

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:20.320
So should we be concerned about the safety&nbsp;
of vote by mail? What do you see as, again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:24.240
taking into consideration all of the different&nbsp;
reasons one might vote one way or the other?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:28.480
What is your message to people about how&nbsp;
it is that they should vote if they really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:33.680
want to feel good about knowing, feeling&nbsp;
that their vote is likely to be counted?&nbsp;

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:40.480
What I tell everyone here is your vote is still&nbsp;
going to be safe and secure. Do not let anyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:45.040
distract you or make you think otherwise.&nbsp;
Our six systems are secure. We have been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:49.280
conducting oversight along with the FBI. We have&nbsp;
been in communication with our supervisor of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:54.640
elections here locally. So if you need to vote by&nbsp;
mail because of health conditions, because you're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.640 --> 00:06:00.960
not here physically, mail that envelope today.&nbsp;
Sign it, seal it, mail it. That's what we're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:06.400
saying. Just send your ballot early if you can&nbsp;
vote early. We start early voting October 19th,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:12.800
and you can do that securely as well. Wear a&nbsp;
mask. Use your hand sanitizer. But vote whatever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:19.280
the plan is for you to vote. Vote. Vote in the way&nbsp;
that's safest for you, for your family vote. Every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.280 --> 00:06:26.080
vote counts. David, in twenty eighteen, I had&nbsp;
a colleague or one of the candidates in Texas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:32.880
who lost her election by nine hundred votes.&nbsp;
Gina Ortiz from Texas, who I think welcome&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:39.520
into Congress in twenty twenty nine hundred votes.&nbsp;
Every single vote counts. Again, if you have your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:47.200
ballot, mail it and sign it, mail it and send it.&nbsp;
It's safe. It's secure. If you can vote in person,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:50.960
vote early. Don't wait until November 3rd.
We have two weeks of early voting here&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.960 --> 00:06:57.600
in Miami Dade and in Monroe County. We can&nbsp;
change the direction of this country. And I,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:03.200
I have a lot of optimism because so many&nbsp;
young people are excited. They're engaged.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:08.160
They're telling their parents their way. Those&nbsp;
deals pretty most pretty much everyone to come&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:12.560
out to vote. And we're going to see that.&nbsp;
We're going to see a huge turnout in 2020.&nbsp;

00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:18.000
So this is speculative. It's just your opinion.&nbsp;
But when do you believe we will know the election&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:24.960
results if we vote decisively in Florida?
If we have a decisive win in Florida, that's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:30.800
going to be a huge indicator that Joe Biden will&nbsp;
be our next president. If Joe Biden wins Florida,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:37.840
of course, that's what I'm referring to.&nbsp;
If we don't know, it could take weeks.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:46.000
And so my recommendation is let all of us expect&nbsp;
that. Don't fret. Don't don't get anxious about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:50.800
it. Let's count every single vote. That's our&nbsp;
democracy. We can be patient. If we've waited&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:58.960
this long, we can wait a couple more weeks. But&nbsp;
my hope is that Florida is so decisive for Joe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:05.040
Biden that that will be a pretty clear indicator&nbsp;
of who's going to take the White House in January.&nbsp;

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:12.240
Yeah, it's it's it's going to be a very, very&nbsp;
interesting election. Extremely high stakes.&nbsp;

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:16.960
Congresswoman Debbie McCaskill, Powell&nbsp;
representing Florida's Twenty Sixth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.960 --> 00:08:21.600
District. Thank you so much for your time.&nbsp;
I really appreciate your joining me today.

